# ZeroOS: GPS on the UART (Cap LoRa-1262's AT6668 at 115200, or a Grove GPS
# unit; gpsd finds the speed). USB GPS dongles are picked up as well.
# gpsd.socket starts gpsd when ZeroShell or meshtasticd connects; without -n
# it only reads the receiver while someone is watching.
DEVICES="/dev/serial0"
GPSD_OPTIONS="-s 115200"
USBAUTO="true"
